### Food Delivery Platform - Review Service (reviews of delivered orders)
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
###
### A customer reviews an order once it is DELIVERED: overall stars, up to 4 tags, a comment and optionally
### stars per dish of that order. Platform admins read the reviews, a summary and the top-rated dishes.
### Run order-service.http and delivery-service.http first: you need an order that is DELIVERED
### (set @orderId below to its id, or run the order flow of delivery-service.http).
###
### Caller identity: the access token's role, CUSTOMER for /reviews, PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/**.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@service = http://localhost:8094
@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@orderId = 1
@menuItemId = 1


### ============================ CUSTOMER ============================

### 1. Customer login -> customerToken
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}" }

### 2. Do I have a review of this order yet? (404 until I write one: the storefront then shows the form)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/reviews/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 3. Review the delivered order
###    tags: DELICIOUS, EXCELLENT, GOOD_SERVICE, FAST_DELIVERY, GOOD_VALUE, GOOD_PACKAGING (at most 4, each once)
###    dishRatings are optional; every menuItemId must be a line of the order, each once.
###    404: unknown order or not yours; 422: not delivered; 409: already reviewed.
# @name createReview
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Hot, fresh and early.",
  "tags": ["DELICIOUS", "FAST_DELIVERY"],
  "dishRatings": [ { "menuItemId": {{menuItemId}}, "rating": 5 } ]
}

### 4. A second review of the same order -> 409
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": {{orderId}}, "rating": 3 }

### 5. Customers cannot read the admin API -> 403
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ============================ ADMIN ============================

### 6. Admin login -> adminToken
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 7. The review list, newest first. Filters: restaurantId, rating (1-5), tag, from, to (yyyy-MM-dd, inclusive)
###    sort: createdAt,desc (default) | createdAt,asc | rating,desc | rating,asc; size at most 50
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/reviews?rating=5&tag=DELICIOUS&from=2026-01-01&sort=createdAt,desc&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8. Summary: number of reviews, average (one decimal) and how many reviews per star
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/reviews/summary?from=2026-01-01
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9. Top-rated dishes (size at most 12): best average first, then most ratings.
###    The picture and category come from catalog-service; without it the dish still shows, with the saved name.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/reviews/featured-dishes?from=2026-01-01&page=0&size=3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================ DIRECT (without the gateway) ============================

### 10. Swagger UI: http://localhost:8094/swagger-ui.html ; health:
GET {{service}}/actuator/health
